Hooks in read.c. The payload's prelude is read before any makefile. A makefile's at lines
and an evaluated text's are rewritten before the parse. The goal make picks from
the first rule is remembered, so a __main__ target can still take its place. The rule
behind an imported target stays here, since it evaluates text through this file's reader.
A load line keeps a leading ./ on its names, since amk's load reads it as the working directory.

